# Layout grammar

Every screen is one of four templates, and every commit action lives in an
ActionBar. Reuse the primitives in `src/components/ui/` instead of building new
chrome.

## The action bar rule

`ActionBar` is the only place a screen commits. It is pinned under the scrolling
body, never inside it, and it clears the keyboard and the home indicator on its
own.

Three slots, always in this order:

- **destructive** (far left) — Delete / Remove. `variant="destructive" size="sm"`.
  Confirm with `window.confirm` before calling the handler.
- **tools** (middle) — secondary actions like Re-estimate or a favorite toggle.
- **primary** (right) — exactly one. Never two primaries on a screen.

There is no Cancel button. Dismissal is the container's job: drag the sheet
handle, tap the dimmer, press Escape, or use the takeover's Close.

Forms live inside the scrolling body, so the submit button is outside the
`<form>`. Wire them with `useId()`:

```tsx
const formId = useId()
// body:   <form id={formId} onSubmit={handleSubmit}>…</form>
// footer: <Button type="submit" form={formId}>Save</Button>
```

## The four templates

| Template | Primitive | Use for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Composer sheet | `Sheet` (`size="tall"`) | Anything that creates or edits data |
| Task takeover | `Takeover` | Flows that own the viewport: camera, voice, favorites |
| Menu sheet | `Sheet` (`size="auto"`) | Short lists of routes; no action bar |
| Browse page | plain page | Lists, charts, summaries |

A browse row carries no action of its own. Tapping the row opens the record;
Edit and Delete live in the sheet that opens from there. Do not put Edit buttons
on cards or list rows.

Errors surface where the action was taken — inside the sheet or takeover, not as
a page-level banner.

## Buttons

Use `Button` from `src/components/ui/Button`. Variants: `primary`, `secondary`,
`ghost`, `destructive`. For file pickers that must stay a `<label>` so iOS opens
native capture, use `buttonClass(...)` with the same variant names.

Use `Field` and `fieldInputClass` from `src/components/ui/Field` for every input
so labels and controls stay identical across screens.
